          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00210:alt:fig-00012-alt",
              "text": "A ketone reacts with sodium borohydride or lithium aluminum hydride, then hydronium ion to form a secondary alcohol."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_17_EC_002.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00013",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00210:alt:fig-00013-alt",
              "text": "An R C O O R prime ester reacts with lithium aluminum hydride, then hydronium ion to form R O H (primary) and R prime O H."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_17_EC_003.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00014",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00210:alt:fig-00014-alt",
              "text": "A carboxylic acid reacts with lithium aluminum hydride, then hydronium ion to form a primary alcohol."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_17_EC_004.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00015",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00210:alt:fig-00015-alt",
              "text": "Formaldehyde reacts with R M g B r, ether, then hydronium ion to form primary alcohol."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_17_EC_005.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00016",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00210:alt:fig-00016-alt",
              "text": "Aldehyde R C H O reacts with R prime M g B r and ether, then hydronium to form secondary alcohol with both R and R prime groups."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_17_EC_006.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00017",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00210:alt:fig-00017-alt",
              "text": "Ketone R C O R double prime reacts with R prime M g B r, ether, then hydronium to form tertiary alcohol with R, R prime, and R double prime."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_17_EC_007.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00018",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00210:alt:fig-00018-alt",
              "text": "Ester R C O O R double prime reacts with R prime M g B r, ether, then hydronium to form tertiary alcohol with R and two R prime."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_17_EC_008.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00019",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00210:alt:fig-00019-alt",
              "text": "A tertiary alcohol reacts with hydronium ion to form an alkene."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_17_EC_009.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00020",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00210:alt:fig-00020-alt",
              "text": "An alcohol reacts with phosphoryl chloride to form an alkene."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_17_EC_010.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00021",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00210:alt:fig-00021-alt",
              "text": "A primary alcohol reacts with Dess-Martin periodinane and methylene chloride to form an aldehyde."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_17_EC_011.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00022",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00210:alt:fig-00022-alt",
              "text": "A primary alcohol reacts with chromium trioxide, hydronium ion and acetone to form a carboxylic acid."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_17_EC_012.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00023",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00210:alt:fig-00023-alt",
              "text": "A secondary alcohol reacts with Dess-Martin periodinane and methylene chloride to form a ketone."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_17_EC_013.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00024",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00210:alt:fig-00024-alt",
